/* ===================================================================
 * capabilities.h -- compile-time platform extension capability flags
 * ===================================================================
 *
 * This header normalizes the "<EXT>_SUPPORTED" presence flags declared by
 * the platform config (config/<platform>/rvtest_config.h) into 1/0 boolean
 * macros named "<EXT>_AVAILABLE", usable both in `#if` and as a value in
 * `if (...)` (e.g. to gate a test or emit TEST_SKIP).
 *
 * Design notes (read before editing):
 *
 *  1. rvtest_config.h is AUTO-GENERATED by riscv-unified-db (udb-gen). The
 *     normalized <EXT>_AVAILABLE macros therefore live HERE, in a separate
 *     hand-maintained file, and must never be added to rvtest_config.h
 *     (they would be wiped on the next regeneration).
 *
 *  2. rvtest_config.h is force-included into every C and assembly
 *     translation unit by common/Makefile.common (-include). capabilities.h
 *     is force-included the same way, right AFTER rvtest_config.h, so the
 *     <EXT>_SUPPORTED flags are already visible here. Do NOT `#include
 *     "rvtest_config.h"` from this file: CONFIG_DIR is not on the -I search
 *     path, only reachable through the absolute -include.
 *
 *  3. <EXT>_SUPPORTED is defined with NO value (e.g. `#define F_SUPPORTED`).
 *     Consequently the Linux-kernel IS_ENABLED() token trick does not work,
 *     and `#if F_SUPPORTED` is invalid ("no expression"). The robust form is
 *     the `#ifdef` guard below that derives an explicit 1/0.
 *
 *  4. This file must stay preprocessor-only (no C types or declarations) so
 *     it remains safe to force-include into assembly as well.
 *
 *  5. Extension support is config-DECLARATION driven: a suite that gates on
 *     an extension must be launched on a simulator/HW whose config declares
 *     it. Do NOT probe at runtime (misa reads or instruction traps) -- that
 *     is fragile and has produced false negatives before.
 *
 * To add a capability, copy one block and change the extension name. Keep the
 * list curated to the extensions tests actually gate on.
 * =================================================================== */

